: Setup self-test. Loads the board and the self-test firmware, gives the
: sensor a known value, and runs long enough for the firmware to report.
:
: The check scripts run this and read the CHECK lines from the serial output.
: Run it by hand with:
:
:   renode --console --disable-xwt verify/verify.resc

mach create "verify"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @boards/nucleo_f401re.repl

: The board carries no sensor, because the real one does not. The self-test
: needs one to prove the I2C path works, so it brings its own rather than
: putting a part on everybody's board that is not on the board in their hand.
machine LoadPlatformDescription @verify/sensor.repl

showAnalyzer sysbus.usart2 Antmicro.Renode.Analyzers.LoggingUartAnalyzer

sysbus LoadELF @verify/verify.elf

: 25 degrees, so the firmware's reading can be compared against something
: known. It will read back 24.99 - see the 'sensor-value-quantisation' row of
: divergences.json.
sysbus.i2c1.si7021 Temperature 25
sysbus.i2c1.si7021 Humidity 50

emulation RunFor "0.05"

: Reported separately from the firmware's own output, because this is the
: simulator's view of the pin rather than the program's view of the register.
echo "CHECK ledstate"
sysbus.gpioPortA.led State
